      "message": "feat(app,ui): fixture plates - a parametric grid/dowel plate, fixtures placed at grid holes\n\nA built-in, parametric fixture (tooling) plate in the fixture library,\nfollowing the built-in vise pattern: a generated solid-slab mesh placed\nthrough InsertFixture, its grid riding FixtureDef (plate::PlateLink).\n\n- Plate: length/width/thickness, hole grid (pitch X/Y, first-hole\n  offset), thread, optional dowel lattice and counterbores; refused by\n  name when nonsensical. Presets: 12 x 12 in, 300 x 300 mm, 400 x 300 mm\n  and one sized from the 770MX machine file's table; \"on the table\"\n  centres a plate on the setup machine's table.\n- Grid names: rows lettered along +Y from A, columns numbered along +X\n  from 1, A1 nearest the plate frame's origin corner.\n- PlaceOnPlate: any fixture at a grid hole or on a dowel pair, standing\n  on the plate top, turned by a yaw; the place is recorded, MoveFixture\n  carries a plate's fixtures (transitively) in its one undo step, and\n  SetPlate re-seats them on the new grid. Unknown locations, gaps,\n  overhangs, cycles and bad turns are refused by name.\n- SetPlateGrid: an imported plate's grid from its detected holes (the\n  Detect holes rule), regular or staggered, with gaps named.\n- Project file: optional `plate` / `on_plate` keys read leniently\n  (dropped and logged, never a failed load); no version bump.\n- MCP: add_fixture_plate, set_fixture_plate, place_on_plate,\n  detect_plate_grid, get_plate_grid.\n- UI: \"Add fixture plate…\" dialog, plate rows, the grid-location\n  picker, \"Detect plate grid\", and viewport hole markers.\n\nFixes #819\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
