      "message": "feat(app,ui): mod vises - fixed and adjustable jaw blocks on the plate grid\n\nA plate-mounted modular vise is two jaw-block fixtures bolted to a\nfixture plate's grid (#819): a fixed block on a named hole, and an\nadjustable block on the nearest hole clear of the stock, slid along its\nslots until its face touches the stock. One undoable PlaceModVisePair\nplaces both as riders of the plate (moving it carries them, deleting it\nlets go of them); each is a meshed fixture judged by the existing\nfixture laws. Refusals by name: out of the slots' reach, off the plate,\nno grid, no stock, stock in the fixed jaw or beside the jaws, bolts\nbetween holes, an off-quarter turn, nonsense figures.\n\nGeneric presets of our own (1 in 3/8-16, 2 in 1/2-13, 50 mm M12 grids);\nan optional, leniently read `mod_jaw` key in the project file; MCP\nadd_mod_vise_pair; \"Add mod vise pair...\" on a plate's Fixtures row.\nDual-station blocks and edit/re-fit are split off to #832.\n\nFixes #820\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
