      },
      "message": "fix(app): a plate edit never pushes a mod vise jaw into the stock\n\nPR #833 review blocker: SetPlate re-seats every rider on its named hole\n(keeping a jaw block's fitted slide) while the stock stays put, so a\npitch change could silently leave a jaw inside the stock (pitch Y - 2:\nthe adjustable face 16 mm in; + 2: the fixed face 4 mm in).\n\n- SetPlate refuses, by name with the side and the depth, an edit that\n  puts a mod vise block's clamping face into the stock or deeper\n  (modvise::reach::face_gap, in the block's frame against the stock\n  box); a face lifted off the stock is a warning (re-fit is #832).\n- SetPlate clash-checks every re-seated rider, and the plate's new slab,\n  against parts and stock as MoveFixture does\n  (fixture_clash::after_fixture_shape); SetPlate::warning, surfaced as\n  MCP set_fixture_plate \"warning\". This also closes the gap for plain\n  riders from #823.\n- The placed-pair status line states the slide in document units.\n- Decision notes: plate edits vs. the stock; body_height must cover the\n  (counterbored) bolt heads.\n\nPinned by mod_vise_plate::a_plate_edit_that_pushes_a_jaw_into_the_stock_is_refused_by_name,\nmod_vise_plate::a_plate_edit_that_keeps_the_jaws_clear_is_accepted_and_undoes_exactly,\nfixture_plate_riders::an_edited_plates_riders_are_clash_checked_where_they_land,\nfixture_modvise_tests::the_placed_status_states_the_slide_in_document_units.\n\nRefs #820\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
